    <h1>Sheinderman Reflection</h1>
    <p>Seeking universal usability in the Shneiderman’s 8 Golden Rules is one that feels the most absent from my micro-project page. There aren't many features that novices would understand if they see my micro-project page as it does require some experience to understand what it is.

The rule that would most improve my sketchbook interface would be Strive for Consistency, as I need to think of a design interface where it matches with everything that is interactable while making it pleasant to look at.

The hardest to apply would be to prevent errors, there is no way to completely control this without testing and bug fixes every detail. 

Keeping users in control is contradicting because it doesn't leave a lot of room for users to make a lot of choices in the first place, as there is nothing.
